      "PandaStack is the rare entry that is both a hosted sandbox service and a self-hostable engine: the repository describes itself as the whole engine rather than a demo, licensed Apache-2.0, with Terraform examples, a GCP self-hosting guide, and an Apple Silicon path for running the stack locally. The architecture is Firecracker microVMs where every create restores a baked per-template snapshot, so startup cost is a snapshot restore rather than a cold boot, and forks are copy-on-write at about 400 ms on the same host. Hibernation is the other interesting choice: state goes to disk, active vCPU and RAM metering stop, and hibernated-state storage is currently free, which makes long-lived idle agents cheap. The metered rates are mid-pack — $0.054 per active vCPU-hour and $0.0162 per GiB-hour of working-set memory, so a busy 1 vCPU / 1 GiB sandbox is $0.0702 per hour — and every plan fee converts 1:1 into usage credit, which is a fairer shape than a fee plus markup. Limits are the main caveat: 8 vCPU per sandbox on all plans, a hard one-hour lifetime on Free, and no published statement of the isolation beyond the microVM boundary.",
