        "The boundary is KVM: each clone is a separate VM with its own kernel, not a container sharing the host kernel. Forks inherit the template's physical pages through copy-on-write and allocate private pages only on write; KSM merges identical pages that diverge and reconverge, and virtio-balloon returns idle memory to the host. The project documents no egress allowlist, per-fork network policy or API layer, so network control and multi-tenant accounting are for the operator to build around it.",
      operatingSystems: ["Linux guests on a Linux KVM host"],
