    overview:
      "DevPod is the pragmatic answer to Codespaces lock-in: keep the devcontainer.json your team already writes, but run it wherever you like. The client is the whole product. You install the CLI or desktop app, add a provider such as Docker, Kubernetes, SSH or a cloud VM, and `devpod up` clones the repository, builds the devcontainer and wires your IDE to it; the same command moves the workspace between local and cloud. VS Code and the full JetBrains suite connect directly, and anything else can attach over SSH. Prebuilds, git and Docker credential sync, and automatic shutdown of idle workspaces cover the operational gaps that made hosted environments convenient. The price is that DevPod deliberately has no opinion about isolation or fleet policy: there is no control plane to enforce egress rules, no snapshot or fork, and a local Docker provider is still a shared kernel. Teams that need audited multi-tenant sandboxes want Coder or a microVM vendor underneath; teams that want their own reproducible dev boxes without a per-seat hosted bill get a strong fit.",
