      networkIsolation:
        "The Seatbelt profile leaves the network open, so this is a filesystem and identity boundary rather than an egress one. It denies all writes outside the sandbox home, the shared workspace and temporary directories; denies reads under /Users except the sandvault user's home and the shared workspace; blocks mounting and unmounting disks, raw disk devices and packet-capture devices; and denies /Library/Keychains except System.keychain. The separate standard user account cannot modify system files and has no access to mounted or network drives. Chrome is launched with --no-sandbox because macOS cannot nest its per-page sandbox, so a Chrome exploit would inherit the sandbox user's access. There is no per-host allowlist or credential proxy.",
